Z||000005||88formula||05-11-2001||04:36 PM||||You need to be more specific about the problem. Is the engine new or used? What rpm does the vibration happen at and does it increase in frequency with higher rpm. Does it feel like one or two cylinders are not firing? Did you just install this motor or has it run fine and all of a sudden this happened?<P>It’s like going to the doctor and telling him I hurt but not telling him were or when. <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||ferrari_momo||05-11-2001||04:56 PM||||wow, thanks for the help guys.  well, the car was done professionally.  it ran fine as 2.8 prior to 3.4 conversion.  the mechanic is a friend of mine.  he said that the injectors are probably the problem or the cause of this vibration.  it will vibrate at idle but ok if i rev the motor at about 1300 RMP.  i am not sure if the vacuume is leaking or electrical problems. <BR>well, if i want to get the most out of 3.4 what do i do?  get different injectors?  i am using K&N filter, replaces gas filter too. the exhaust system is fairly new( about 30,000 miles).  the motor had 20,000 miles.  the fly wheel was from the 2.8 (88GT).  hmm, what could be wrong?  thanks agian people  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
